WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
Your trusted motion equations
come with one strict condition.

2
00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.340
The acceleration must not change.

3
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:10.140
Now picture an object
that starts from rest,

4
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.560
with an acceleration that climbs steadily,

5
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:16.040
from negative to positive, over 2 seconds.

6
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.420
At first it moves backwards.

7
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.030
Then it turns, and heads
off forwards ever faster.

8
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.240
Those familiar equations no longer apply.

9
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.870
So how can you work out where it ends up?

10
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.530
In this mission, you'll shrink
a time interval towards zero,

11
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.390
and watch an average velocity
become an instantaneous one.

12
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.470
Then you'll split a curved
path into directions,

13
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.130
and treat each direction on its own.

14
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.930
Your mission: show how to find where an
object ends up when its acceleration keeps

15
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:46.760
changing.
